In tonight's edition, a Nigerian court disqualifies a leading presidential candidate, adding fresh complications for the electoral process two months before the election. Also, tens of thousands have fled across the border into Kenya as deadly ethnic clashes in southern Ethiopia intensify. And having fled conflict and violence, members of the first Refugee Youth Olympic Team are chasing Olympic dreams at Dakar 2026.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a47ac0fe-d95e-11f1-b71a-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/DN00001654-VOD-00013405.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a47ac0fe-d95e-11f1-b71a-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/DN00001654-VOD-00013405.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ba1d186c-d95e-11f1-90b4-8d6c950560fb</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 21:22:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Clarisse FORTUNÉ</dc:creator></item><item><category>Across Africa</category><title>Navi Pillay: Fighting violence with justice</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/navi-pillay-fighting-violence-with-justice</link><description>
From the International Criminal Court to Africa’s place in the global justice system, the stakes are high. In an exclusive interview, Nobel Peace Prize winner, Navi Pillay will discuss international justice . She says it it must not be held hostage to political power, as Donald Trump targets the ICC. What does this showdown mean for Africa?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/667b0550-d933-11f1-80f6-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8219ec1f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/667b0550-d933-11f1-80f6-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8219ec1f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">591b06f6-d92b-11f1-8c2e-8394b69f450d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 16:12:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Clarisse FORTUNÉ</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>South Africans eager to vote as local elections put failing services in focus</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-south-africans-eager-to-vote-as-local-elections-put-failing-services-in-focus</link><description>
South Africans voted on Wednesday, November 4, in local elections. Nearly 30 million people were eligible to cast their ballots, with corruption, failing infrastructure and the deterioration of essential services among the key issues shaping the vote. FRANCE 24's correspondent Eunice Masson reports from the ground.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/921c672a-d8fd-11f1-be33-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261104-214433-214559-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/921c672a-d8fd-11f1-be33-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261104-214433-214559-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">96bb51d8-d8fd-11f1-8b37-73ea55f09c4f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 10:48:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Sudan accuses Ethiopia of allowing RSF drone launches from its territory</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-sudan-accuses-ethiopia-of-allowing-rsf-drone-launches-from-its-territory</link><description><![CDATA[
Sudan accused Ethiopia of allowing the paramilitary Rapid Support Forces (RSF) to launch drones from its territory. What does this allegation reveal about the RSF's military capabilities and foreign backing? FRANCE 24 spoke to Ali Mahmoud Ali, a Sudan researcher at ACLED, the Armed Conflict Location & Event Data Project, which monitors conflicts worldwide.
]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fc973e92-d900-11f1-8fa9-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-f0e4f3cb.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fc973e92-d900-11f1-8fa9-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-f0e4f3cb.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f4b9f68a-d8fe-11f1-b7d6-ff25c3707b82</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 10:42:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ethiopian families fleeing conflict face difficulties with food access</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-ethiopian-families-fleeing-conflict-face-difficulties-with-food-access</link><description>
A renewed conflict in Ethiopia has led to the displacement of thousands of civilians. But after years of war in the country and heavy budget cuts, humanitarian organisations have all but left many of the camps for internally displaced people, leaving many without food or health care. FRANCE 24's correspondent Tom Canetti reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0f0bfba2-d902-11f1-aa75-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-184d92ca.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0f0bfba2-d902-11f1-aa75-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-184d92ca.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b89e5ca8-d8ff-11f1-a231-53fbbc465d42</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 10:38:41 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>South Africans vote in key municipal elections</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/south-africans-vote-in-key-municipal-elections</link><description>
In tonight's edition: South Africa's ruling ANC party faces a crucial test as millions vote to elect municipal governments. Also, Ethiopia has expelled six Sudanese diplomats amid accusations it's allowing the paramilitary RSF to launch drone strikes from its territory. Plus an ongoing humanitarian crisis deepens in Ethiopia, where renewed fighting has displaced thousands.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/17ac9550-d8fd-11f1-bb42-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-ca811725.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/17ac9550-d8fd-11f1-bb42-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-ca811725.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">02241562-d896-11f1-8fe6-47e26de2f8b0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 21:26:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Jean-Emile JAMMINE</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>DR Congo residents sue Chinese mining giant for widespread pollution</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-dr-congo-residents-sue-chinese-mining-giant-for-widespread-pollution</link><description>
In Kolwezi, the mining capital of the Democratic Republic of Congo, local residents are suing a huge Chinese mine and the government for environmental pollution. It will be one of the most important cases the country has seen. FRANCE 24's correspondent Emmet Livingstone reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e7e763c-d839-11f1-8445-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-db69893a.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e7e763c-d839-11f1-8445-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-db69893a.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d90130d8-d832-11f1-9559-5d98673f8ffb</guid><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 10:22:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>30 million South Africans registered to vote across nine provinces</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-30-million-south-africans-registered-to-vote-across-nine-provinces</link><description>
In South Africa, around 30 million people have registered to cast their votes across the country's nine provinces. The economy is at the forefront of the November 4 local elections. The spotlight is on Gauteng, a province long plagued by governance challenges. FRANCE 24's correspondent Eunice Masson reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d62a5192-d836-11f1-a337-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d1cbe76a.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d62a5192-d836-11f1-a337-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d1cbe76a.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">971fc2f4-d834-11f1-9e28-ab65d8803149</guid><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 10:20:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Sudanese Arab refugees face hostility and distrust after fleeing to Chad</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-sudanese-arab-refugees-face-hostility-and-distrust-after-fleeing-to-chad</link><description>
Thousands of Arab Sudanese who have arrived in Chad after fleeing fighting at home are facing mistrust and hostility from fellow Sudanese refugees. Fighters linked to the Rapid Support Forces, whose ranks are largely drawn from Sudan’s Arab communities, have been accused of repeatedly targeting civilians from other ethnic groups. FRANCE 24's Harold Girard reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/89c17344-d836-11f1-adf9-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d102c735.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/89c17344-d836-11f1-adf9-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d102c735.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">93821308-d835-11f1-ba00-fdb2d595ac82</guid><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 10:18:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Washington excludes South Africa and Rwanda from US duty-free trade deal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-washington-excludes-south-africa-and-rwanda-from-us-duty-free-trade-deal</link><description>
South African and Rwandan exporters are weighing potential job losses and squeezed margins after Washington decided to exclude them from the AGOA program, the African Growth and Opportunity Act, ending the countries' duty-free access to the US market. Economists warned against "alarmist" reactions to the exclusion and argue the broader economic fallout will likely be limited.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/933c5318-d835-11f1-bb26-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4c57a384.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/933c5318-d835-11f1-bb26-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4c57a384.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4873bc02-d832-11f1-b9e4-91147f919c10</guid><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 10:15:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>South Africa braces for some job losses as AGOA ends</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/south-africa-braces-for-some-job-losses-as-agoa-ends</link><description>
In tonight's edition: Rwanda and South Africa will lose their duty-free access to the US market after being excluded from the AGOA trade programme. Also, South Africans head to the polls amid water shortages and frustration with local services. Plus in DR Congo's mining capital Kolwezi, residents are taking on one of the country's largest Chinese-owned mines, accusing it of poisoning their environment. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8fa1c4ec-d829-11f1-8fed-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-67cae517.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8fa1c4ec-d829-11f1-8fed-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-67cae517.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d05b5f42-d7cb-11f1-9e68-df2784793caa</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 21:18:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Clarisse FORTUNÉ</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Senegal's opposition-dominated parliament rejects revised budget bill</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261103-senegal-powerful-opposition-rejects-crucial-budget-bill</link><description>
Senegal's powerful opposition party Pastef led by former presidential candidate Ousmane Sonko on Tuesday rejected a revised version of the country's budget, leaving the west African nation's new bailout programme with the International Monetary Fund hanging in the balance. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c9ea1580-d781-11f1-a558-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26146434698018.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c9ea1580-d781-11f1-a558-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26146434698018.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9b2303f4-d783-11f1-a76d-493bbb872455</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 12:40:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c9ea1580-d781-11f1-a558-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26146434698018.jpg">© Misper Apawu, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Uganda withdraws its troops from Somalia as fight against rebels persists</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-uganda-withdraws-its-troops-from-somalia-as-fight-against-rebels-persists</link><description>
Kampala announced on Monday it had begun pulling its troops out of Somalia. Uganda was the first country to send deployments to help Mogadishu when the African Union set up an international military mission in 2007 to battle al-Shabab extremist rebels. But what is prompting Kampala to withdraw its troops now, as the battle against the militants continues? FRANCE 24’s Georga Calvin Smith is joined by Horn of Africa geopolitical analyst Anwar Abdifatah Bashir.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/afe44278-d77c-11f1-bdcf-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-0fbd1c25.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/afe44278-d77c-11f1-bdcf-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-0fbd1c25.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7dc42ee6-d76a-11f1-a073-dd8d7db66563</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 11:50:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>South Africans demand security and basic services as they vote in local elections</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-south-africans-demand-security-and-basic-services-as-they-vote-in-local-elections</link><description>
High crime rates and a lack of basic services are causing concern among many of South Africa’s 29 million registered voters. Water shortages and unreliable electricity supplies have also become symbols of municipal failures, angering voters and eroding support for the ruling African National Congress. The municipal elections on November 4 will offer a glimpse into whether these frustrations are shifting political loyalties. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1a578556-d76f-11f1-9761-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-88604f9b.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1a578556-d76f-11f1-9761-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-88604f9b.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6832511a-d76b-11f1-be53-3b6562aab2c2</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 11:39:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>DR Congo opposition figure Prince Epenge arrested for spreading fake news</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-dr-congo-opposition-figure-prince-epenge-arrested-for-spreading-fake-news</link><description>
DR Congo senior opposition leader Prince Epenge has been arrested and transferred to prison. He is being held on charges of spreading fake news. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Kinshasa, Emmet Livingstone, has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1d681bce-d770-11f1-8511-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-f8ca607c.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1d681bce-d770-11f1-8511-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-f8ca607c.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">17777a24-d76c-11f1-a06b-4db6169f869b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 11:27:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Chadian farmers suffer from intensifying drought and take stock of their losses</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-chadian-farmers-suffer-from-intensifying-drought-and-take-stock-of-their-losses</link><description>
In Chad, Wadi Fira is one of the two regions hardest hit by the drought. Just a few kilometres outside Biltine, the regional capital, farmers take stock of their devastating losses. FRANCE 24's Harold Girard reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8f41b250-d770-11f1-93ea-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a6e71a7e.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8f41b250-d770-11f1-93ea-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a6e71a7e.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c9ada01a-d76c-11f1-bc64-ab76f6ce3dd0</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 11:26:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Uganda withdraws troops from peacekeeping mission in Somalia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/uganda-withdrawing-troops-from-peacekeeping-mission-in-somalia</link><description>
In tonight's edition: Uganda starts drawing down troops just days after the UN ends its political mission in Somalia. Also, upcoming municipal elections in South Africa risk solidifying growing political fragmentation. Plus the drought gripping Chad could be the country's worst in more than 40 years. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4ec52b46-d769-11f1-adab-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a2259aeb.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4ec52b46-d769-11f1-adab-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a2259aeb.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">15d625ee-d703-11f1-bde7-2b1cb8998ece</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 21:24:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>UN’s peacekeeping mission in disputed Western Sahara ends after 35 years</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261101-un-s-peacekeeping-mission-in-disputed-western-sahara-ends-after-35-years</link><description>
The 35-year-old UN peacekeeping mission ⁠in the disputed Western ​Sahara region came to an end Sunday after the Security Council failed to ​renew its mandate. Morocco, which claims the region as its own, welcomed the decision, while its opponents from the Algeria-backed Polisario Front called it "unacceptable".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0bfbe8ea-a712-11ec-a859-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/8013915005001.jpg.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0bfbe8ea-a712-11ec-a859-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/8013915005001.jpg.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3766e2a6-d632-11f1-8508-ff00334a173f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 20:37:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0bfbe8ea-a712-11ec-a859-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/8013915005001.jpg.png">© Mohamed Siali, EFE</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Senegal hosts first Olympic event on African continent</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/senegal-hosts-first-olympic-event-on-african-continent</link><description>
Youth Olympics make history with first African Games in over 130 years, opened by Senegal’s president in Dakar. 136 Senegalese athletes are competing, supported by 6,000 local volunteers.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75a22272-d5da-11f1-80a7-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-101101-101232-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75a22272-d5da-11f1-80a7-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-101101-101232-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7a838ef2-d5da-11f1-a6e6-cd8963e0e204</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 09:58:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Youth Olympic Games kick off in Dakar</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/youth-olympic-games-kick-off-in-dakar</link><description>
The 2026 Youth Olympic Games have officially kicked off in Senegal. Crowds gathered for Saturday's opening ceremony, featuring hundreds of drummers and dancers celebrating Senegalese and wider African culture, in keeping with the Games' motto: “Africa welcomes, Dakar celebrates”. It is the first-ever Olympic sporting event to be held on the African continent, but comes as Senegal faces an economic crisis. The country's president has said he wants to turn sport into an “economic and social engine”. The Games also come amid a government crackdown on LGBTQ+ people. Nearly 3,000 teenagers from more than 200 countries are competing in around a dozen sports, including athletics, beach wrestling and a five-a-side version of baseball. Jean-Loup Chappelet, Professor at Lausanne University and Olympics specialist, shares further insights.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/083e7dee-d5d9-11f1-a7c9-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/dakar-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/083e7dee-d5d9-11f1-a7c9-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/dakar-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">93cf92c0-d5d5-11f1-9cad-e9fc0a89d0a7</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 09:49:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Senegal kicks off Africa's first ever Olympics with Youth Games</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261031-senegal-hosts-africa-s-first-ever-youth-olympic-games</link><description>
The 2026 Youth Olympic Games opened on Saturday in the Senegalese capital Dakar in the first-ever Olympics to be held on African soil. It comes as the continent seeks a bigger role in international sporting competitions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a1fd18bc-d55e-11f1-bc0b-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-31T185551Z-1026728015-UP1EMAV1GL175-RTRMADP-3-OLYMPICS-YOUTH-OPENING.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a1fd18bc-d55e-11f1-bc0b-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-31T185551Z-1026728015-UP1EMAV1GL175-RTRMADP-3-OLYMPICS-YOUTH-OPENING.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">df068bcc-d508-11f1-8850-2bda8f827ba6</guid><pubDate>Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:37:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a1fd18bc-d55e-11f1-bc0b-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-31T185551Z-1026728015-UP1EMAV1GL175-RTRMADP-3-OLYMPICS-YOUTH-OPENING.jpg">© Misper Apawu, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>First Youth Olympic Games take place in Africa</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/first-youth-olympic-games-in-africa</link><description>
In tonight's show: The Senegalese capital Dakar is hosting the first Olympic event ever held in Africa, welcoming nearly 2,700 athletes for the 2026 Youth Olympic Games. Also, South Africa's local elections are set for November 4, with the African National Congress facing growing pressure over its record in local government. Finally, we're joined by Muse L'Artiste, who's reconnecting to her roots with her latest EP "Heritage" bringing her father's compositions back to life.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9239705c-d4a9-11f1-aacb-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4f9e60a5.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9239705c-d4a9-11f1-aacb-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4f9e60a5.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ca5497e8-d4a7-11f1-ae3f-a1a5294fe4d4</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:48:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Clarisse FORTUNÉ</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russia recruits Africans to fight in Ukraine, families seek answers</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/russia-recruits-africans-to-fight-in-ukraine-families-seek-answers</link><description>
While African leaders and Russian officials gather to discuss security, trade and political cooperation at the Africa-Russia summit, one sensitive issue is notably absent from the agenda: the recruitment of Africans to fight for Russia in Ukraine. More than 1,400 Africans have been enlisted since 2023. In Tunisia, concern is growing as the families of several men who travelled to Russia for work or study are still searching for answers about the fate of their loved ones. FRANCE 24's team in Tunisia reports. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3f32cba-d44b-11f1-873d-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-dc16521b.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3f32cba-d44b-11f1-873d-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-dc16521b.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d93e6f8a-d444-11f1-aaf8-15429d64cfb0</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:06:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>At least 60 Christians killed in Ethiopia amid rising religious violence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-at-least-60-christians-killed-in-ethiopia-amid-rising-religious-violence</link><description>
At least 60 Christians have been killed in Ethiopia in what the Orthodox Church has declared as religious violence. It is still unclear who was behind the attack, with rebels and local government blaming each other. Around 20 houses have been burned down, as FRANCE 24's correspondent Tom Canetti reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b965392-d44c-11f1-9c71-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-46bebd36.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b965392-d44c-11f1-9c71-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-46bebd36.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d327128a-d446-11f1-94a8-c5ddd4874f79</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:01:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Senegal gears up for historic 2026 Youth Olympic Games in Dakar</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-senegal-gears-up-for-historic-2026-youth-olympic-games-in-dakar</link><description>
The International Olympic Committee is upbeat just 24 hours before competition gets under way at the 2026 Youth Olympic Games in Senegal. Venues are ready to host the first-ever Olympic event on the African continent. FRANCE 24's correspondent Aminatou Diallo reports from the ground.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b53b7c32-d44d-11f1-ada0-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6cca01f2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b53b7c32-d44d-11f1-ada0-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6cca01f2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">31bfe5a2-d44b-11f1-aad5-6df4798b8782</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:58:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Tanzania: 2025 election violence still traumatises, one year on</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-tanzania-2025-election-violence-still-traumatises-one-year-on</link><description>
Tanzania is marking the first anniversary of a bloody election that left many traumatised. The October 29, 2025 election, in which President Samia Suluhu Hassan won with 98 percent of the vote after most of the opposition was excluded, triggered days of protests that security forces brutally suppressed. Many government critics say they still fear abduction, arbitrary arrest and politically motivated prosecutions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6cfc6408-d44e-11f1-b7a8-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5fb1d914.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6cfc6408-d44e-11f1-b7a8-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5fb1d914.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bb5f5748-d44b-11f1-822e-7fb8cd2f846a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:55:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Tunisians drawn into Russia's war in Ukraine</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tunisians-drawn-into-russia-s-war-in-ukraine</link><description>
In tonight's edition: Concern is growing in Tunisia as the families of several men who travelled to Russia for work or study are still searching for an answer about the fate of their loved ones forcibly conscripted to the war in Ukraine. Also, a year after Tanzania's controversial election, fear hasn't faded. And Dakar is ready to make history, as the first Olympic event ever held on African soil gets underway this weekend. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0e3b7f9e-d453-11f1-b60c-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-0a159d9a.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0e3b7f9e-d453-11f1-b60c-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-0a159d9a.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">598bbdc8-d3e1-11f1-b9a1-ffdbf081a42b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:48:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Clarisse FORTUNÉ</dc:creator></item><item><category>Across Africa</category><title>Across Africa: Real estate scams on the rise in Ivory Coast</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/across-africa-real-estate-scams-growing-in-ivory-coast</link><description>
This week in Across Africa: In Ivory Coast, a severe housing shortage has fuelled demand for land, creating opportunities for fraudsters selling fake properties and non-existent plots. Also, Kenya's women are changing the game. From the track to the boxing ring, female athletes are delivering some of the country’s biggest sporting successes. Plus Addis Ababa pushes ahead with ambitious plans to become East Africa's clean-energy powerhouse.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd846a12-d470-11f1-ad0f-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-334a8094.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd846a12-d470-11f1-ad0f-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-334a8094.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e72d9274-d3ae-11f1-894b-f5d04db9dbe9</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:43:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Clarisse FORTUNÉ</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>DR Congo: A centre celebrates the discharge of last Ebola patients</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-dr-congo-a-centre-celebrates-the-discharge-of-last-ebola-patients</link><description>
Medical staff and residents at a treatment centre in Ituri danced and sang to celebrate a first since May: the centre is no longer treating any confirmed Ebola cases.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aed2a692-d3ba-11f1-b307-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-RDC-Ebola-10.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aed2a692-d3ba-11f1-b307-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-RDC-Ebola-10.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cf178a9e-d3ba-11f1-8363-1bb562418fc6</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:13:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Putin seeks to expand ties with African countries at Russia-Africa summit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-putin-seeks-to-expand-ties-with-african-countries-at-russia-africa-summit</link><description>
Russian President Vladimir Putin on Wednesday hosted dozens of African leaders at a Russia-Africa summit, part of Moscow’s efforts to expand its influence across the continent. The Russia-Africa summit marks a renewed Kremlin effort to bolster ties with a continent of nearly 1.6 billion people that is increasingly assertive on the global stage. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c0aa0bc-d37f-11f1-bedb-811458fcf026/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-29T091823Z-1533690092-RC2WCOA2IVT4-RTRMADP-3-RUSSIA-AFRICA-SUMMIT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c0aa0bc-d37f-11f1-bedb-811458fcf026/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-29T091823Z-1533690092-RC2WCOA2IVT4-RTRMADP-3-RUSSIA-AFRICA-SUMMIT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f9182ffe-d37b-11f1-a580-6f50dc8232ce</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:32:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
